# The vendored notification client is hash-pinned by
# scripts/client_manifest.json and must stay byte-identical to the canonical
# copy at ../_shared/notify_client.py. Pin it to LF: a CRLF copy normalises
# back on a Linux checkout, stops matching its pin, and fails CI for a reason
# that has nothing to do with the code.
iptv_checker/notify_client.py text eol=lf

# The vendored report page furniture is hash-pinned by
# scripts/chrome_manifest.json and must stay byte-identical to the canonical
# copy at ../_shared/report_chrome.py, which Stream-Mapparr also vendors. Same
# reasoning as above: a CRLF copy normalises back on a Linux checkout and stops
# matching its pin.
iptv_checker/report_chrome.py text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
